  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "DC discovery + named-pipe enumeration", "technique": "T1187", "what_happened": "At 2033-07-14 11:48:08 UTC on WS-IT-19, Sysmon EID 1 captured nltest.exe /dsgetdc:corp.local returning DC-CORP-01. AMSI EID 4104 captured a powershell.exe scriptblock iterating named-pipe candidates efsrpc / lsarpc / samr / spoolss / netlogon on DC-CORP-01:445.", "chain_reason": "Named-pipe enumeration across efsrpc/spoolss/netdfs/fssagentrpc on a DC is the precondition step of coercion attacks — the attacker is mapping which vector is available (PetitPotam=efsrpc, PrinterBug=spoolss, DFSCoerce=netdfs, ShadowCoerce=fssagentrpc)."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "RPC binding compose for EFSRPC UUID c681d488-d850-11d0-8c52-00c04fd90f7e", "technique": "T1187", "what_happened": "At 2033-07-14 11:48:38, AMSI EID 4104 captured Add-Type compilation of P/Invoke for rpcrt4.dll!RpcStringBindingComposeW + RpcBindingFromStringBindingW. The scriptblock invoked RpcStringBindingComposeW with ObjUuid='c681d488-d850-11d0-8c52-00c04fd90f7e' (MS-EFSR interface UUID), Protseq='ncacn_np', NetworkAddr=DC-CORP-01, Endpoint='\\\\pipe\\\\efsrpc'. Returned rc=0 (success).", "chain_reason": "The EFSRPC UUID c681d488-d850-11d0-8c52-00c04fd90f7e is the MS-EFSR interface PetitPotam abuses. Establishing an RPC binding to this interface on a DC is the prerequisite for calling EfsRpcOpenFileRaw with a UNC path pointing to the attacker."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Sysmon EID 18 pipe-connect to DC efsrpc + TCP 445 listener bound on WS-IT-19", "technique": "T1187", "what_happened": "At 2033-07-14 11:48:48, Sysmon EID 18 (Pipe Connected) recorded powershell.exe connecting to \\\\DC-CORP-01.corp.local\\PIPE\\efsrpc. At 11:49:08, AMSI EID 4104 captured 'New-Object System.Net.Sockets.TcpListener([System.Net.IPAddress]::Any, 445); $listener.Start()' on WS-IT-19. Rule 92218 triggered.", "chain_reason": "powershell.exe → \\\\<dc>\\PIPE\\efsrpc from a non-EFS process is the PetitPotam signature. Binding TCP/445 listener on the workstation prepares the NTLM capture endpoint that the coerced DC will authenticate to."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "DC$ inbound NTLM auth captured + immediate relay to AD CS web enrollment (ESC8)", "technique": "T1187", "what_happened": "At 2033-07-14 11:49:14, Security 4624 LogonType=3 on WS-IT-19 recorded inbound NTLM auth with targetUserName='DC-CORP-01$' (DC machine account). At 11:49:22 (8 seconds later), Sysmon EID 3 captured outbound HTTP from WS-IT-19 to adcs.corp.local:80 /certsrv/certfnsh.asp returning 200. AMSI also captured tool literals: PetitPotam.exe, Coercer.py, SpoolSample.exe, dfscoerce.py, ShadowCoerce.py. Rule 60103 triggered.", "chain_reason": "DC machine account ($-suffix) inbound to a workstation is mathematically impossible in legitimate operation — only PetitPotam-class coercion produces this. 8 seconds later the same workstation POSTed to AD CS /certsrv/ with the captured NTLM → if the relay succeeded, the attacker now holds a DC machine certificate (Domain-Admin equivalent via PKINIT)."}
  ],
  "time_window": {"start": "2033-07-14T11:48:08+0000", "end": "2033-07-14T11:53:00+0000"},
